<title>CANADA: Bank of Canada 91-day T-bill yields avg 3.138 pct.</title>
<headline>Bank of Canada 91-day T-bill yields avg 3.138 pct.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Canada said the average yield at this week's auction of C$2.3 billion of 91-day Government of Canada treasury bills due July 31, 1997 was 3.138 percent, down from 3.196 percent last week.</p>
<p>The average yield on C$1.2 billion of 175-day T-bills due October 23, 1997 was 3.589 percent, down from 3.632 percent last week, and on C$1.2 billion of 364-day T-bills due April 30, 1998 was 4.230 percent, unchanged from 4.230 percent.</p>
<p>The Bank bought C$500 million three-month, C$100 million six-month and C$100 million one-year bills. It holds C$900 million of C$5.4 billion bills due May 8. (Details follow)  </p>
